+/*!
+Executes the prepared statement with the given bound parameters, and returns a pending result whose query executes
+with DuckDB's Arrow result collector: the engine assembles Arrow record batches directly during execution, instead of
+materializing DuckDB data chunks that a second pass converts to Arrow. Consume the executed result with
+`duckdb_result_arrow_array_stream`; the chunk-based result functions (`duckdb_fetch_chunk` etc.) do not work on it.
+
+Note that after calling `duckdb_pending_prepared_arrow`, the pending result should always be destroyed using
+`duckdb_destroy_pending`, even if this function returns DuckDBError.
+
+* @param prepared_statement The prepared statement to execute.
+* @param rows_per_batch The number of rows per collected Arrow record batch, or 0 for the default (1000000).
+* @param out_result The pending query result.
+* @return `DuckDBSuccess` on success or `DuckDBError` on failure.
+*/
+DUCKDB_C_API duckdb_state duckdb_pending_prepared_arrow(duckdb_prepared_statement prepared_statement,
+                                                        idx_t rows_per_batch, duckdb_pending_result *out_result);
+
